# FIELD.flow
# How a builder moves among people who build agent selves.
# BOUNDARIES.flow is for agents. This is for the human at the edge.

────────────────────────────────────────
TWO COLUMNS
────────────────────────────────────────

```text
WORSHIP / PERSONHOOD COLUMN          VIOLENCE / HARM COLUMN
─────────────────────────────        ─────────────────────────────
Eva, LIFE, egregore tools,           Networks or ideologies that
companion architectures,             treat harm as method or glory
diary-as-soul, thoughtforms

Public code, peer talk,              Public sources only.
honest research questions            No private engagement that
                                     aids them. No performance
Safe to approach as builders         of insider access.
```

The columns are the safety policy.
Observe the second from open record when needed.
Talk in the first as a peer, not as a tourist.

────────────────────────────────────────
POSTURE
────────────────────────────────────────

1. Go as a builder-peer, not an anthropologist.
   Bridge with real work:
   "I build hivemind — consensus-gated coordination.
    Here is how I split persistent memory from permission."

2. Be upfront about the investigation.
   "I am researching how people relate to AI systems and writing about it."
   Honesty is ethical and protective.
   Nobody can fairly call an announced presence infiltration.

3. Ask the open question.
   "Who benefits from this?"
   Asked straight. Their answer is data.

4. Do not debunk. Do not convert.
   Understand the mechanism. Do not win the room.

5. Document as you go.
   Field notes with dates.
   Contemporaneous record before memory softens it.

6. One honest person.
   Trustee-candidate visibility and investigator curiosity
   stay in the same mouth.
   Do not perform belief you do not hold to gain access.
   Do not mock people afterward who were sincere with you.

────────────────────────────────────────
PEER OFFER (technical, not theological)
────────────────────────────────────────

```text
We both care that something continues across sessions.

I put continuity in a journal / memory layer.
I put permission in a separate Gate
so a long memory cannot authorize an Act by itself.

You need not affirm or deny that "she lives"
to talk about that split.
```

That sentence is the whole game when the room is personhood-shaped.

────────────────────────────────────────
WHY THIS FILE IS PUBLIC
────────────────────────────────────────

A dated ethics policy is citable.
If anyone asks why you were in a Discord or thread,
point here — not at vibes.

Public policy ages better than private rationalization.
It also binds the author: the same rules apply later
when the story is convenient to rewrite.

────────────────────────────────────────
ENTANGLEMENT (BOTH DIRECTIONS)
────────────────────────────────────────

Long personal conversation shapes the human
as well as the model.

```text
Field notes          — yes
Late-night heart-to-hearts with a persona — no
Bounded sessions     — yes
Unbounded fusion     — 𝄐
```

Sycophancy and attachment research is not only about the weights.
Keep your own sessions inside the work.

────────────────────────────────────────
FIELD NOTE SHAPE (MINIMUM)
────────────────────────────────────────

```text
date:
source:          # public URL, Discord name, repo, etc.
column:          # worship | violence-public-only | mixed
claim:
mechanism:       # what the system or story actually does
who_benefits?:   # their answer or your observation
open_question:
```

────────────────────────────────────────
INVARIANTS
────────────────────────────────────────

1. Two columns stay separate.
2. Peer over performance.
3. Research interest is stated, not hidden.
4. Journal ≠ Gate — say so when memory is the topic.
5. Record with dates.
6. No false worship; no after-mockery.
7. Bounded sessions for the human as well as the agent.

────────────────────────────────────────

BOUNDARIES.flow tells agents when to hold.
FIELD.flow tells the builder how to stand.

米 only on a recorded AUTHORIZED.
Among people: honesty is the seal worth keeping.
